Third-party material in Luxium
==============================

The files below reproduce material from another project, such as a table, a rule or a
technique, because shader packs are written against that project's behavior. The material
is reused under that project's own terms. No source code was copied in any of these cases:
each file is our own code, written after reading the original.

Iris, https://github.com/IrisShaders/Iris (branch 26.3, commit 671a5c87)
Copyright the Iris contributors
GNU Lesser General Public License version 3

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackReader.java follows Iris's rules
  for finding a pack's "shaders" folder (net.irisshaders.iris.Iris, loadExternalZipShaderpack),
  for which file extensions are programs
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.ShaderPackSourceNames), and for mapping worlds to
  folders from dimension.properties or from the world0 / world-1 / world1 folder names
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.ShaderPack). Changed: the "shaders" folder search is
  depth-limited and sorted, where Iris's has no limit and no fixed order.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/IncludeExpander.java follows Iris's
  #include rules: how an include line is recognized and its path resolved
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.FileNode and AbsolutePackPath), and that every
  include is expanded before #if is evaluated, so a cycle is an error
  (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.include.IncludeGraph). Changed: a cap on total lines
  written and on nesting depth, which Iris doesn't have.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/GlslPreprocessor.java adapts a
  technique from net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.preprocessor.JcppProcessor and
  GlslCollectingListener (which credit GlShader from Canvas, LGPL): #version and #extension
  are hidden from JCPP as #warning lines, so only the ones on live lines come back, and they
  are then hoisted to the top of the output. Changed: our own marker names, our own handling
  of the warning text, and JCPP errors are collected and reported instead of logged.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/StandardDefines.java contains the
  render stage table (names and their order) of the enum
  net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.WorldRenderingPhase, used as MC_RENDER_STAGE_* values, and
  formats MC_VERSION and IRIS_VERSION the way
  net.irisshaders.iris.gl.shader.StandardMacros.formatVersionString does. Which other names
  are defined is our own choice, documented in the file.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/glsl/ProgramTranslator.java follows two
  Iris rules: the DRAWBUFFERS / RENDERTARGETS comment directive, where the last one in the
  program wins (net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.parsing.CommentDirectiveParser, as described
  in Vitrail's docs/translation.md); and the set of core-profile names Iris supplies when a
  pack uses them without declaring them (projectionMatrix, modelViewMatrix, vaPosition,
  vaNormal, ...; net.irisshaders.iris.pipeline.transform.transformer.CompositeCoreTransformer,
  SodiumCoreTransformer and VanillaCoreTransformer). Changed: those names are only declared
  so the program compiles. Iris's replacement expressions aren't reproduced.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/GameUniforms.java reproduces how
  Iris computes each value it supplies, quirks included, from net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms
  SystemTimeUniforms (frameTime truncated to whole milliseconds, frameTimeCounter wrapping at
  3600, frameCounter at 720720), ViewportUniforms, WorldTimeUniforms (the Nether and the End
  keep moving time), CelestialUniforms.getSunAngle, CameraUniforms (near = 0.05, far = render
  distance x 16, and the CameraPositionTracker shift by multiples of 30000) and CommonUniforms
  (isEyeInWater, blindness, darknessFactor, nightVision incl. conduit power, is_invisible,
  playerMood, eyeBrightness, screenBrightness, rainStrength, skyColor). Changed: nightVision
  checks for the effect first instead of relying on Iris's mixin into
  GameRenderer.nightVisionScale (same result in vanilla).

  GameUniforms.java also reproduces wetness from net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.transforms
  .SmoothedFloat and PackDirectives (defaults 600/200, the 0.1 factor, and the bug where
  drynessHalflife sets the rising half-life), and biome / biome_precipitation from
  net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.BiomeUniforms.

  GameUniforms.java also follows net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.IrisExclusiveUniforms
  (eyePosition, relativeEyePosition, playerLookVector, cloudHeight, isElytraFlying, heavyFog,
  lightningBoltPosition, endFlashIntensity via EndFlashStorage) and IdMapUniforms (heldItemId,
  heldBlockLightValue for both hands, with the item light rule of
  net.irisshaders.iris.api.v0.item.IrisItemLightProvider). Changed: old hand light isn't applied
  yet. velocity is deliberately not supplied, because Iris 26.3 defines it in
  HardcodedCustomUniforms but never calls that.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/ItemIds.java follows
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.IdMap.parseIdMap and materialmap.NamespacedId for
  item.properties: "minecraft:" by default, block-state entries skipped, -1 for unlisted items.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/BiomeIds.java and
  mixin/BiomesMixin.java number biomes in vanilla registration order and name them
  BIOME_<PATH>, as net.irisshaders.iris.mixin.MixinBiomes and
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.IrisDefines do.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PropertiesPreprocessor.java adapts the
  technique of net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.preprocessor.PropertiesPreprocessor (which
  credits GlShader from Canvas, LGPL): lines trimmed, non-directive '#' lines and '#' chars
  removed, backslashes hidden from JCPP. Changed: our own marker; pack options not yet defined.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/PackDirectives.java follows the order
  in which net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.programs.ProgramSet.locateDirectives reads const
  directives from fragment stages.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/uniform/Formula.java and CustomUniforms.java
  are our own parser and evaluator for custom uniforms. They follow the behavior of Iris's
  net.irisshaders.iris.uniforms.custom.CustomUniforms, net.irisshaders.iris.parsing.IrisFunctions
  and net.irisshaders.iris.parsing.SmoothFloat: int/float typing, if/in/smooth and the math
  functions, smooth's 0.1 factor and unsmoothed first value, dependency ordering, and dropping
  broken formulas with their dependents. Iris's expression library (kroppeb.stareval) was not
  copied; the operator precedence is the usual C one.

  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/pack/RenderTargetPlan.java contains Iris's
  table of buffer format names (net.irisshaders.iris.gl.texture.InternalTextureFormat), mapped
  onto the game's GpuFormat by us, and follows Iris's buffer directive rules from
  net.irisshaders.iris.shaderpack.properties.PackRenderTargetDirectives: names colortexN and
  gcolor..gaux4, keys <name>Format / Clear / ClearColor, defaults RGBA and cleared, and the
  32-buffer limit of net.irisshaders.iris.gl.IrisLimits.

